    "question": {
      ":question/id": "398766d1-ef72-58f5-b068-456be1ac76b5",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "What is the sum of the leading entries of the $1\\text{st},$ $2\\text{nd},$ and $3\\text{rd}$ rows in the matrix $A,$ given below?\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 9 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The first non-zero entry of each row (from left to right) is the leading entry. \n\nTherefore, the leading entries of the $1\\text{st},$ $2\\text{nd},$ and $3\\text{rd}$ rows of $A$ are $9,$ $3,$ and $5$, respectively.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 9 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, the answer is $9+3+5=17.$",
